            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0403" n="1237" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/385</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-23T20:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 23, 7.04 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10235. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 645. Foreign Office and Wallenberg do not think that the form of adhesion
                    proposed in my 560, Embassy’s 10003, May 11, 5 p.m. <pb facs="0404" n="1238"
                        xml:id="pg1238"/> and modified by your 511, Department’s 7834, May 20, 6
                    p.m., is sufficient, as it will not provide for undertaking in the tonnage
                    agreement concerning bunkering and licensing of vessels. Would you agree to
                    following clause being added to the approved form of adhesion: “and the War
                    Trade Board during the currency of the above-mentioned agreement [will issue
                    licenses] for the bunkering of Swedish vessels in accordance with the terms of
                    the tonnage agreement and will adhere to the terms of such tonnage agreement
                    which is a part of the general agreement”?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
